<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ForeCastTab — the body of the ForeCast window: the SPC outlook (card + day / product / opacity) with
     its legend, plus NowCast's GHOST rows around it. One of three mode bodies (see Controls/Windows/TemporalWindow,
     registered once per mode); the window supplies the surface, the title and the pin, so this is content only.
     ⚠️ The file keeps its "Tab" name from when the three were tabs of one Timeframe window. It is the same
     control, unchanged by the split; renaming all three would be churn. Bound to the coordinator
     MapViewModel; every real control here drives ViewModel.Outlook.

       ┌──┐ ForeCast                    │ MDT 4/5                  ← THE NAME ROW (Past/Now's, matched): square =
       │██│ Day 1 · Wed Sep 2           │ next ~9 min                the HIGHEST category in the shown outlook, in
       └──┘                                                          its SPC colour (blue = no areas); readout =
                                                                     that category + the refresh countdown
       [x] Show NowCast ghost rows                               ← persisted, default off; fixed (doesn't scroll)
       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ ⠿   ░░ ░Storm cells · NowCast░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ │  ← GHOSTS (PanelSection IsGhost): NowCast's
       │ ⠿   ░░ ░Warnings · NowCast░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ │     layers, 25%, drag-only — only while the
       │ …                                                    │     box is on AND NowCast runs. ONE shared
       │ ⠿ ⌄ [x] SPC outlook  ────────●──────   55%           │     Now + Fore order: a drag here moves
       │                                                      │     NowCast's window too, and vice versa
       │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐        │
       │  │ Day 1 · Categorical                      │        │  the card: which outlook is
       │  │ Issued 12:57 PM · Valid → Wed 7:00 AM    │        │  drawn, when SPC issued it,
       │  │ Next ~9 min                              │        │  and the refresh countdown
       │  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘        │
       │  Day      [Day 1 · Wed Sep 2          ▾]             │  ← self-labeling; cascades Product
       │  Product  [Categorical       ▾] [Discussion.]        │  ← opens the Outlook Discussion WINDOW
       │  Cycle    [Latest                     ▾]             │  ← Latest | today's earlier issuances (HELD)
       │  ────────────────────────────────────────────────    │
       │   ■ 2%              Intensity hatching   [✓] Show    │  ← the LEGEND (Primitives/OutlookLegend):
       │   ■ 5%              ╲ CIG1             In Outlook    │     LAST in the section body, so it goes
       │   ■ 10%             ╱ CIG2             In Outlook    │     with the section when collapsed; also
       │   ■ 15%             ╳ CIG3         Not In Outlook    │     hidden when HasLegend is false (None).
       │                                                      │  ← colours | hatching, two equal halves; the
       │                                                      │     hatching half only when the product has
       │                                                      │     intensity groups (status from the CACHED GeoJSON)
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       │ ⠿   ░░ ░Radar · NowCast░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ │  ← ghost (default spot: under the outlook)
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                                             ┃  ← all of the above sits in PanelScroller: a 16 px
                                                                gutter always claimed, thumb ┃ only on overflow

     ONE REAL SECTION, a Primitives/PanelSection (the one header every section in the app wears). SPC outlook
     is open on a first run — it is what the window is for. Open/closed is then PERSISTED ("fore/..." in
     AppSettings.SectionExpanded; ghosts don't persist — they have no body), and so are Day, Product, opacity
     and hatching (ViewModels/Map/TemporalWindowPersistence). Inside it: a summary CARD, then [label | control]
     rows in one aligned 60px column, then the legend.
     ⚠️ The window opens at a FIXED full height, so the layer run SCROLLS inside Primitives/PanelScroller
     (2026-09-30, the same scroller as Past/Now). WinUI's bar is not wanted — see the PanelScroller header.
     ⚠️ THE DISCUSSION IS A WINDOW NOW (Windows/OutlookDiscussionWindow, the Product row's "Discussion."). It
     was an inline collapsed section pinned at the bottom of this body until 2026-10-01 (the user's call).

     ⚠️ THE OUTLOOK HEADER'S BOX IS A LAYER SHOW/HIDE (OutlookViewModel.IsShown), NOT the mode. The mode is
     OutlookViewModel.IsOutlookVisible (MapViewModel.IsForeCast projects onto it), and a tab body never arms
     or clears its own mode — see the last ⚠️ in this header. The box sits UNDER the mode, exactly as
     PastCast's outlook box does.
     ⚠️ GHOST ROWS: ForeCast has no layer order of its own — its outlook lives in the SHARED Now + Fore order
     (MapViewModel's GHOST ROWS block; saved as NowCastLayerOrder). The ghosts are NowCast's layers in the map's
     default spots (LayerOrder.Default); a drag here saves the Now order and the NowCast window follows
     (LayerOrderChanged). A ghost's box mirrors the real show/hide, inert.

     ⚠️ THE CARD COSTS NO VIEW-MODEL WORK. Its three lines are OutlookViewModel state that was already
     being computed and shown nowhere — the title, the issued/valid line, and the refresh countdown. See
     the card region in that class.

     ⚠️ THE LEGEND LIVES INSIDE THE OUTLOOK SECTION, last, exactly as in PastCast (both host the shared
     Primitives/OutlookLegend). It used to be its own star row outside the section; the user's call
     (2026-09-28) was one shape for both windows, so collapsing the section now takes the legend with it.
     The Day row is the same ComboBox in both windows too.

     ⚠️ THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO REAL RADAR SECTION HERE, unlike Past and Now (the radar row is a GHOST,
     inert). Radar opacity is a GLOBAL value, and those two windows can only get away with sharing a control
     for it because their modes are mutually exclusive. ForeCast COEXISTS with NowCast, so a live slider here
     would be a second control writing the same value with both windows on screen.

     ⚠️ Opacity is DISABLED while Product is None or the box hides it (ShownOnMap) — the same rule the
     PastCast outlook and the storm-report dots follow.

     ⚠️ This tab does NOT turn ForeCast on or off; that is the ForeCast key in the bottom bar's centre
     cluster. A tab body configures a mode, the key runs it. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.ForeCastTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:conv="using:Anvil.Converters"
             xmlns:local="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:models="using:Anvil.Models"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <conv:BoolToVisibilityConverter x:Key="BoolToVis"/>
        <conv:HexToBrushConverter x:Key="HexToBrush"/>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- ⚠️ NOT top-aligned, unlike the Past/Now roots: TemporalWindow hands this the full window height, and
         the star row is the SCROLLER, which fills it. -->
    <Grid x:Name="Root">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- THE NAME ROW: square · ForeCast over the day │ highest risk -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- "Show NowCast ghost rows" -->
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>    <!-- the layer run in PanelScroller: fills the space, scrolls when it can't -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ===================== THE NAME ROW — NowCast's / PastCast's header, matched (2026-10-07) =====================
             The window's chrome carries no title any more (TemporalWindow); the name shows once, here.
             ⚠️ THE SQUARE = the HIGHEST category the shown outlook contains, in its SPC colour (DATA, never themed —
             the feed's own fill, else the catalog's), as NowCast's square is the warnings feed's staleness. No areas
             / nothing shown = PastCast's blue (OutlookViewModel.NoAreasFill). Its tooltip names the category.
             ⚠️ Padding LEFT 0 / RIGHT 4 = the section stack's edges — PastCast's + NowCast's rule; change together.
             No TemporalHeaderMinHeight: there are no tiles or card under it to line up. -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" Padding="0,12,4,12">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="22"/>   <!-- the square -->
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>    <!-- ForeCast over the day -->
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- hairline · highest risk over the countdown -->
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <Border Grid.Column="0" CornerRadius="5,0,0,5"
                    Background="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderSquareFill, Mode=OneWay, Converter={StaticResource HexToBrush}}"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderSquareTip, Mode=OneWay}"/>
            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Margin="12,0,12,0" Spacing="2" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <TextBlock Text="ForeCast" FontSize="30" FontWeight="SemiLight"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderDayText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
            </StackPanel>
            <!-- The CLOCK's spot: the highest risk at 30 SemiLight (the PastCast window range's size), the countdown
                 under it. "No areas" / "No outlook" dims to 40%, PastCast's placeholder rule. -->
            <Border Grid.Column="2" BorderThickness="1,0,0,0" Padding="12,0,0,0"
                    BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
                <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center" Spacing="2">
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderRiskText, Mode=OneWay}"
                               FontSize="30" FontWeight="SemiLight"
                               Opacity="{x:Bind PeakOpacity(ViewModel.Outlook.HasPeak), Mode=OneWay}"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.OutlookNextUpdateText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
        </Grid>

        <!-- GHOST ROWS box: NowCast's layers as dimmed, drag-only rows around the outlook, so you can say where the
             outlook draws among them (ONE shared Now + Fore order). Persisted, default off; the rows show only
             while NowCast runs too (MapViewModel's GHOST ROWS block). -->
        <CheckBox Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,0,0,8" Content="Show NowCast ghost rows"
                  IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShowNowCastGhostRows, Mode=TwoWay}"
                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="List NowCast's layers here, dimmed, so you can drag the outlook among them (shown while NowCast is on)"/>

        <!-- ===================== THE LAYER RUN: one contiguous block of layer sections ===================== -->
        <!-- ⚠️ In Primitives/PanelScroller, like Past/Now's sections — present whether or not the outlook overflows
             yet (the user's call, 2026-09-30): the gutter is always claimed, the thumb only draws on overflow.
             Margin right -12 BLEEDS the gutter into the window's 16 px body margin (the PanelScroller header).
             ⚠️ A StackPanel of its own (like Past/Now's "Sections"): the outlook + NowCast's ghost rows are ONE
             run. With the ghosts hidden the outlook is alone, so its grip shows but a drag never starts
             (PanelSection needs 2 visible). Reordered → SetLayerOrder(Now): the shared Now + Fore order. -->
        <prim:PanelScroller Grid.Row="2" Margin="0,0,-12,0">
        <StackPanel x:Name="Sections" VerticalAlignment="Top" Spacing="8">

        <!-- ===================== GHOSTS: NowCast's layers, in the map's default spots ===================== -->
        <!-- Drag-only (IsGhost); boxes mirror the real show/hides, inert. Collapsed = still in the run, so the
             saved order keeps their places. The XAML order IS the map default (LayerOrder.Default). -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Storm cells · NowCast" LayerId="cells" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormCells.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Storm reports · NowCast" LayerId="reports" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Warnings · NowCast" LayerId="warnings" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Warnings.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Watches · NowCast" LayerId="watches" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Watches.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Mesoscale discussions · NowCast" LayerId="mds" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Discussions.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>

        <!-- ===================== SPC OUTLOOK: the card, then the selectors ===================== -->
        <!-- LayerId → the grip. The header box is SHOW/HIDE (Outlook.IsShown, persisted) — NOT the mode, which
             is the bottom bar's ForeCast key; hiding keeps Day / Product. Works whatever the product, None
             included (PastCast's rule). Opacity greys while hidden or None: nothing drawn to fade. -->
        <prim:PanelSection x:Name="OutlookSection" Header="SPC outlook" LayerId="outlook" IsExpanded="True"
                           Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.IsShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnOutlookHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide the outlook (keeps the day and product you picked)"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.OutlookOpacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ShownOnMap, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Outlook fill opacity (outlines stay solid)">
            <Grid>
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the card -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rule -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the selectors -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the legend: last, so a collapsed section takes it along -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- THE CARD, the same shape as the PastCast outlook's and for the same reason: it is a
                     RESULT, not a preview — there is no Load here, the outlook applies the moment you pick it,
                     so it describes what is on the map right now. That is also why it carries no button. -->
                <Border Grid.Row="0" CornerRadius="8" Padding="13,12"
                        Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CardHeadline, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="15"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CardContext, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="13" Margin="0,4,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.Outlook.CardContext), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CardFooter, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="11" Margin="0,6,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.Outlook.CardFooter), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Grid.Row="1" Height="1" Margin="0,14"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

                <Grid Grid.Row="2" ColumnSpacing="12" RowSpacing="10">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="60"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Day -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Product -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Cycle -->
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- Day: self-labeling ("Day 1 · Sat Jun 14"); changing it cascades the product list.
                         ⚠️ A ComboBox in BOTH windows (PastCast's Day row matches): the live outlook runs to
                         EIGHT days (d4-8 are the extended probabilistic), well past what a SegmentedPicker
                         suits, and one control keeps the two sections identical. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="Day" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                    <ComboBox Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.Days}"
                              DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                              SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.SelectedDayOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="SPC outlook day"/>

                    <!-- Product: the day's outlook types (+ None). The list CASCADES with the day, so it stays
                         a dropdown — its length changes. -->
                    <!-- …and SHARES its row with "Discussion.", which opens the Outlook Discussion window (no row
                         of its own — the user's call, 2026-10-01; PastCast's Product row matches). -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Text="Product" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                    <Grid Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" ColumnSpacing="8">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ComboBox HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ProductOptions, Mode=OneWay}"
                                  DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                                  SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.SelectedOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="Outlook product (None clears the overlay)"/>
                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Content="Discussion."
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HasOutlook, Mode=OneWay}"
                                Click="OnDiscussionClick"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Read SPC's forecast discussion for this outlook in its own window"/>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Cycle: the SAME row as PastCast's (the user's call, 2026-09-30: both outlook sections laid
                         out exactly alike). Latest = the live feed, following every new issuance; an earlier one of
                         today's is fetched from IEM and HELD. Not persisted (see OutlookViewModel). Disabled while
                         None, or when the day has nothing earlier to pick (days 4-8, or before the first issuance). -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Text="Cycle" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                    <ComboBox Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CanPickCycle, Mode=OneWay}"
                              ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CycleOptions, Mode=OneWay}"
                              DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                              SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.SelectedCycleOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="SPC issuance (UTC); Latest follows each new one, an earlier one stays put"/>
                </Grid>

                <!-- THE LEGEND: last in the body. Hides on HasLegend (None, or the layer off); the section's
                     own collapse hides it with everything else. -->
                <prim:OutlookLegend Grid.Row="3"
                                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HasLegend, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    Entries="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.LegendEntries, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    HatchRows="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HatchLegendRows, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    ShowHatching="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ShowHatching, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
            </Grid>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <prim:PanelSection Header="Radar · NowCast" LayerId="radar" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowRadarLayer, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </StackPanel>
        </prim:PanelScroller>
        <!-- (The inline "Forecast discussion" section that sat pinned below here is GONE — SPC's discussion
             moved to its own window, the Outlook Discussion window, opened by the Product row's "Discussion."
             button. The user's call, 2026-10-01.) -->
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
